quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  2,234,"As for those among you who die leaving widows behind, they (i.e. the widows) shall wait by themselves for four months and ten days (after their husband’s death). When they have reached the end of their waiting period, you are not accountable for what they reasonably decide for themselves. Allah is All-Knowing of what you do."
  2,235,"There is no sin upon you in giving such women a hint of a marriage proposal (during the waiting term) or what you may secretly cherish in your hearts. Allah knows that you will be thinking of (proposing to) them. But do not make a secret arrangement with them unless you speak (to them) honourably. Do not confirm the marriage tie until the prescribed term reaches its end. Be aware that Allah knows what is in your hearts, so beware of Him, and know that Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Forbearing."
  2,236,"There is no sin upon you if you divorce your wives while you have not touched them (by consummating the marriage) or settled a dowry for them. (Even if the dowry is not fixed) yet provide for them reasonably: the wealthy according to his means and the poor man according to his capacity, with honourable sustenance. (It is) an obligation on the virtuous."
  2,237,"And if you divorce them before you have touched them (to consummate the marriage), but after you have fixed the dowry for them, (pay) half of what you have previously fixed, unless they waive (their right), or unless the one who holds the marriage tie waives (his right). However, waiving your right (O husbands) is nearer to God-consciousness. So, do not forget generosity towards one another (even in these moments of stress). Indeed, Allah is All-Seeing what you do."
